# Every text file in this tree is LF, and a CRLF file here is not a cosmetic problem.
#
# THE FAILURE THIS PREVENTS, BECAUSE IT IS NOT OBVIOUS. Several tests in src/quality/ parse
# BUILD-STATE.md and docs/FIVE-YEAR-PLAN.md line by line with regexes anchored by `$` — and in
# JavaScript `.` does not match `\r`, which is a line terminator. So a CRLF rewrite of the plan
# makes `/^- \*\*(W\d+)\*\* (.*)$/` match NOTHING: the parser silently found zero of 260 units,
# and because every assertion in plan-ledger.test.ts runs over that list, four tests failed at
# once while the files themselves looked untouched in an editor.
#
# It reached this repo by an editing tool writing files back through Python's text mode on
# Windows, which translates \n to \r\n on write. Normalising here means it cannot be committed
# again regardless of which tool does the writing.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries, so nothing tries to normalise inside them.
*.png binary
*.pptx binary
*.docx binary
*.xlsx binary
